    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YWjtKsLbFBfV3ynQseWxLE)_\n\n## What\nThe 0.85 relative height of #146 made the dashboard boxes misalign. Removed `sp-fonts-dashboard-menu-height` and `sp-fonts-ui-faces`. Instead `sp-dashboard-menu-face` is added to `fontaine-faces` (in the `:config` of the fontaine block, before the first preset is set) and the `t` preset sets `:sp-dashboard-menu-face-height` to 1.0, so the dashboard is back on the grid of the `default` font and a preset can change the height. I read fontaine's source (3.1.0): `fontaine-faces` is a plain list of faces, and a preset reads `:FACE-height` as a multiple of the `default` height. Docs and CHANGELOG updated.\n\nAny other height makes box text and box lines differ in width, so boxes only align at 1.0 unless the layout is moved to pixel widths.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9cVX4xhp367pqb88n)_",
